```

**Map rules**

- `# Current item:` is the live pointer (id, title, short status). Keep it in sync with `.data/MASTERTRACK.md`.
- Items are **C**n (curriculum), **M**n (milestone), or **Capstone**. Number curriculum and milestone ids in design order (`C1`, `C2`, `M1`, `C3`, …). Do not reuse an id.
- Each **curriculum** item has **three or four** skills (`C1.1`, `C1.2`, …). Each skill has a start point and a verifiable end goal. Those skills are the spine of the later `CURRICULUM.md` (one section per track skill).
- **Milestones** sit after every **two** curriculum items. A leftover unpaired curriculum item goes before the capstone with no extra milestone.
- **Capstone** is last. **Uses** lists the curriculum items it depends on (the whole track).
- Milestone and capstone **Steps** are accomplishments, not code and not lesson plans. Do not put solution snippets in the map.
- Do not write `curriculum/CURRICULUM.md` in this file.

## Progress (`.data/MASTERTRACK.md`)

```markdown
# Mastertrack progress

- **Track:** Track title
- **Current item:** C1 — Python foundations
- **Current item status:** not started
- **Flag:** `.data/IN_MASTERTRACK_CURRICULUM` (`on` while a live course is a track step)

## Skills

Status is one of: `not started` · `learning` · `shaky` · `mastered`

| ID | Skill | Status | Note |
|----|-------|--------|------|
| C1.1 | Basic Python data structures | not started | |
| C1.2 | Control flow and functions | not started | |
| C1.3 | Modules, packaging, and tests | not started | |
| C2.1 | ... | not started | |
```

**Progress rules**

- **Current item status** is `not started` · `learning` · `paused` · `complete`.
- One row per **track skill** (`C1.1`, …), not per curriculum lesson. Lesson-level rows stay in `.data/STUDENT.md` only.
- Look up a track skill by **ID**. Update in place; never add a second row for the same ID.
- **Note** is optional and short.
- When a curriculum step is archived, set that step’s track-skill rows to `mastered` or `shaky` from how independently they finished the matching sections. Do not copy lesson IDs into this table.
